open Ideal IsLocalRing

universe u v w

namespace Algebra

section

variable {k : Type u} [Field k]
variable {Λ : Type v} [CommRing Λ] [IsArtinianRing Λ] [IsLocalRing Λ] [Algebra k Λ]
variable {p : ℕ} [Fact p.Prime] [CharP k p]

/- Domain-style sampling for Lemma 16.11.1.

Primary domain: directed approximation of an Artinian local `k`-algebra by `k`-subalgebras inside
a fixed ambient algebra.

Sampled owner declarations in the surrounding project/mathlib style:
* `Algebra.exists_directed_smooth_subalgebra_family` from `Lemma_10_158_11.lean`, stated
  directly on a family `S : ι → Subalgebra k K` with explicit `Directed` and `iSup` witnesses;
* `Algebra.isGeometricallyRegular_of_directed_iSup_subfields` from
  `Lemma_10_166_5.lean`;
* `Algebra.EssFiniteType` from `Definition_9_6_6.lean` / mathlib;
* `Subalgebra.iSupLift` and the directed-supremum API from mathlib.

Best owner abstraction: the `Algebra` namespace theorem-level owner on a family
`S : ι → Subalgebra k Λ`. The stagewise Artinian/local/flat and essentially-finite-type
hypotheses, the maximal-ideal compatibility, and the condition `iSup S = ⊤` are properties of
that owner family, not primitive wrapper data.

Layering:
* `source-facing`: existence of a directed approximation family with the stated stage properties;
* `core/canonical`: `Subalgebra k Λ`, `Algebra.EssFiniteType`, and the directed `iSup` API;
* `bridge/view`: the interpretation of this directed supremum as a filtered-colimit presentation.
-/

-- Proof sketch: choose directed Artinian local `k`-subalgebras of `Λ` generated by finite pieces of
-- the residue field together with generators of the maximal ideal; use the finite-dimensionality of
-- `H_1(L_{K/k})` for `K = ResidueField Λ` to arrange compatible sections and descend the
-- coefficients to finitely generated intermediate fields; then apply the Artinian local criterion
-- for essential finite type over the residue field and take the directed union over all such
-- finitely generated intermediate fields.
/-- Lemma 16.11.1: let `k` be a field of characteristic `p > 0` and let `Λ` be an Artinian local
`k`-algebra. If the first cotangent homology `H_1(L_{K/k})` of the residue field
`K = ResidueField Λ` is finite-dimensional over `K`, then `Λ` is the directed union, equivalently
the filtered colimit, of Artinian local `k`-subalgebras `A ⊆ Λ` such that each inclusion
`A → Λ` is flat, the extended maximal ideal of `A` is the maximal ideal of `Λ`, and `A` is
essentially of finite type over `k`. -/
theorem exists_artinianLocalSubalgebraApproximation
    [FiniteDimensional (ResidueField Λ) (Algebra.H1Cotangent k (ResidueField Λ))] :
    ∃ (ι : Type w) (S : ι → Subalgebra k Λ)
      (hdir : Directed (· ≤ ·) S)
      (hArt : ∀ i, IsArtinianRing (S i))
      (hLoc : ∀ i, IsLocalRing (S i))
      (hFlat : ∀ i, Module.Flat (S i) Λ)
      (hMax : ∀ i,
        let _ : IsLocalRing (S i) := hLoc i
        Ideal.map (algebraMap (S i) Λ) (maximalIdeal (S i)) = maximalIdeal Λ)
      (hEssFiniteType : ∀ i, Algebra.EssFiniteType k (S i)),
      iSup S = (⊤ : Subalgebra k Λ) := sorry

end

end Algebra
